From ac2cb376a5af1d3ce19da8c8c4bd98af16a49fec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 05:29:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 229/638] chrome: enable portable desktop features on AROS
 [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-phase-4-browser-link

AI_STATUS: done

ROOT_CAUSE: Chrome linked portable media preview, mirroring, payments, spelling, WebUI preload, and keyboard call sites on AROS while their implementations remained restricted to established desktop platform predicates.

FIX_REASON: Admit AROS to source sets that contain no Linux, DBus, X11, or native-handle assumptions, select the existing Ozone keyboard path, and define the WebUI result move constructor already declared by its public contract.

SCOPE: Chrome browser/browser-ui GN source selection, Views webview Ozone selection, and one missing WebUI special-member definition.

VALIDATION: All 36 newly selected compile/archive edges completed; //chrome:chrome final link inventory fell from 64 to 47 unresolved OS contracts; git diff --cached --check passes.

RISK: low to medium; these are existing cross-platform feature implementations, with actual media/device availability still governed by Chromium service capabilities.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap;
---
 chrome/browser/BUILD.gn                                       | 4 ++--
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn                                    | 2 +-
 .../ui/webui/top_chrome/webui_contents_preload_manager.cc     | 1 +
 ui/views/controls/webview/BUILD.gn                            | 2 +-
 4 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

